title: 'EPMB: determine the signed base deposit at registration'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    The base deposit of a signed submission is now charged once, when the submitter calls
    `register`, and is not re-computed afterwards. `submit_page` only holds or releases the change
    in the per-page part of the deposit. Previously, every `submit_page` re-computed the
    whole deposit from the current queue length, so the held amount depended on registrations made
    by other accounts after the submitter registered.

    No storage migration is needed. Submissions in flight at upgrade keep their held deposit, and
    later page changes only move the per-page part.
crates:
- name: pallet-election-provider-multi-block
  bump: major
